            "legacyType": "String"
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": {
        "legacyType": "User",
        "type": "none",
        "httpStatus": 204,
        "note": "No body. A new account is of no use to a caller until the address is confirmed, and legacy proves the point: its resolver returns a User, its own frontend selects only { id } from it, and that id is one of the faked ones. Answering with nothing also makes the silence rule structural instead of maintained — a registration for an address already in use gets the identical empty 204, so there is no shape for the two paths to differ in and no fabricated identifier for a client to keep."
